      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the fourth term of the sequence \\(3^0, 3^0 + 3^1, 3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2\\), we start by writing each term in its expanded form.\n\n1. The first term (\\(k=3^0\\)) is:\n   \\[\n   3^0 = 1\n   \\]\n\n2. The second term (\\(k=3^0 + 3^1\\)) is:\n   \\[\n   3^0 + 3^1 = 1 + 3 = 4\n   \\]\n\n3. The third term (\\(k=3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2\\)) is:\n   \\[\n   3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 = 1 + 3 + 9 = 13\n   \\]\n\n4. The fourth term (\\(k=3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3\\)) is:\n   \\[\n   3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3 = 1 + 3 + 9 + 27 = 50\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of the fourth term of the sequence is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
